# AgentFlow notes

> This section is appended by ZCode-AgentFlow to the resolved agent context
> (`control_root/resolved-agent-context.md`); it is NEVER written into the
> repository's own `AGENTS.md`. It is **context only** — guidance for the
> planning/review models — and is NOT a security allowlist.

## Verification command shape (v1)

Each task declares structured verification commands (never free-form shell
strings):

```json
{ "program": "pytest", "args": ["-q"], "cwd": ".", "timeout_sec": 120 }
```

A command has one of three `kind`s, governed by two DISTINCT structured
allowlists from `config.yaml` (`verification.program_allowlist` /
`interpreter_allowlist`):

- `executable`     — the `program` itself must be in `program_allowlist`.
- `cmd_script`     — a `.bat`/`.cmd` script path inside the worktree, run via
                     `cmd.exe`; the interpreter must be in `interpreter_allowlist`.
- `bash_script`    — a `.sh` script path inside the worktree, run via `bash`;
                     the interpreter must be in `interpreter_allowlist`.

If a script kind is not supported in the current version, the schema/config
**explicitly rejects** it rather than claiming support. Unsafe metacharacters
(`& | < > ^ % !`) in program/args are rejected; the program+args are always
passed to `subprocess` as a list (never concatenated into one string).

## v1 scope: single task per run

A v1 plan carries **exactly one task**. A multi-task goal is rejected at plan
validation (the planner-result wrapper surfaces `NEEDS_USER_INPUT` / `BLOCKED`),
never silently truncated to `tasks[0]`.

## Allowlists are config, not Markdown

The security source for verification is the structured `program_allowlist` /
`interpreter_allowlist` in `config.yaml`. This file (and any repo `AGENTS.md`)
is **context only** — never parsed into an executable allowlist, never trusted
as a security boundary.
